Ian, Got it to plot briefly by following #5 to install from Rforge.
But ran Contingency tables and crashed. Now unable to plot again. I
will try a clean install and get back to you.

We really like the product at PSU, but when we tell students to
install on various platforms there are problems.  e.g.   "got JGR with
Deducer working at home yesterday.  It requires version 2.13.0 of R.
It doesn't work with the 2.13.0 version of R, 64 bit though. I saw one
funny thing happening when I was in the Plotting part of the program.
If I had JAVA working on a webpage, the Plotting didn't work and froze
in the GUI.  Kind of strange."
So although we like the package very, very much we cannot recommend it
to students since they have trouble installing it.  And we do too.
I will get back to you later this weekend after a clean re-install of
R2.13
-spicer

